These weights implement a classic negative‑feedback controller: cart position and velocity receive negative gains to pull the cart toward the origin, the sine of each pole angle is weighted negatively so the force pushes opposite to the lean, and both angular velocities are also weighted negatively to damp motion. The cosine terms and constraint force are set to zero because they add little linear error information, and the bias is zero to avoid a constant drift. This combination should produce stronger corrective actions while keeping the cart centered, thereby extending episode length and moving the return toward the high‑reward optimum.
